    "case_id": "amb1-case05-family-archive",
    "focal_region": {
      "annotated_sentence_text": "[Turn 4 USER]\ne029\tThat sounds more abstract than the actual relationship.\ne030\tTomas found and protected most of these boxes when our grandmother's apartment was cleared.\ne031\tHe feels he took responsibility while I now act like the archive belongs to a process I control.\ne032\tI did spend hundreds of hours organizing it, but I joined later.\ne033\tIf I insist on a catalog-first approach, he may hear that his years of care count less because they were not systematic.\n[Turn 4 ASSISTANT]\ne034\tThe labor histories matter.\ne035\tFormal organization can accidentally become a claim to authority, just as physical custody and early rescue can become one.\ne036\tYou may need to recognize those contributions explicitly before negotiating the exhibition, not because recognition settles final say but because otherwise each procedural disagreement carries an older argument about ownership.\ne037\tA shared decision process will feel hollow if either of you believes the other's kind of care is treated as secondary.\n[Turn 5 USER]\ne038\tThe cultural center says the exhibition can be small—perhaps twenty items—and they are comfortable showing captions as provisional or including two versions of a story.\ne039\tThey need a commitment in a month to reserve the spring slot.\ne040\tTomas sees that flexibility as answering my concern.\ne041\tI feel relieved and also suspicious of my relief, because twenty items still create a frame.\ne042\tWhatever we choose becomes “our family” to strangers who will not see the rest.\n[Turn 5 ASSISTANT]\ne043\tAny selection will create a frame, including waiting until the catalog is complete.\ne044\tThe center's flexibility reduces pressure to pretend certainty, but it does not eliminate authorship.\ne045\tYou could define the exhibition more narrowly—as twenty objects about how family memory is assembled—rather than as a representative family history.\ne046\tThat may be honest, though it risks making the process the subject when Tomas wants the lives and migration stories to remain central.",
